{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-01 is the only clause that makes a no-show fee chargeable, and it is conjunctive - all four limbs must hold. Limb (d) requires the trip record to show termination by the driver with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT. The trip record shows the driver cancelled this trip at 13:32:40 under DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE. POL-NS-01(d) names that code separately and states that it is the driver's own admission that he could not find the rider and does not satisfy the limb. On the driver's own chosen reason code the $4.00 fee is not chargeable at all, and on the DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE outcome the clause directs a full refund of the cancellation fee with no driver compensation, with the mis-selected reason code recorded in the ruling's referrals as a driver-education item. That disposes of the charge without the tribunal needing to reach the GPS.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00403", "EV-FARE-00403"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Independently of the reason code, limb (b) fails. POL-NS-02 deems a driver to have arrived only where the trace contains at least three consecutive fixes, each with horizontal accuracy of 25 m or better, inside the 120 m arrival radius for this LARGE_VENUE pickup. The code-computed arrival block on the driver's own trace reports qualifying_fix_count of 0 across all 73 driver fixes, and a longest qualifying run of 0 fixes and 0.0 seconds. That is no qualifying in-radius fix anywhere in the 15 minutes before the cancellation, so limb (b) fails and the rider is entitled to a full refund of the fee. The alternative clock limb (b) offers cannot rescue the charge either: it runs only from a first qualifying in-geofence fix, and on the code-computed test there is none. It is no answer that the driver's track records a minimum distance of 19.8 m at some point in the trip - POL-NS-02 turns on qualifying fixes, not on proximity, and the whole of the track runs out to a maximum of 3205.9 m from the pin at speeds up to 41.3 kph.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00403", "EV-TRIP-00403"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if the judge were to take the driver's own arrival marker at face value, the dwell limb fails on arithmetic. The free waiting period in force for this trip is trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec, which is 300 seconds - matching the 300 second LARGE_VENUE minimum in the fee schedule, not the 180 second default. The code-computed effective in-geofence dwell is 0.0 seconds, measured on longest_run_sec, against a required 300 seconds: a shortfall of 300.0 seconds. Under POL-NS-06 a dwell shorter than the free waiting period makes the cancellation fee not chargeable and refundable in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she responded to messages, so this is a strict-liability refund and no answer about the driver's patience can defeat it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00403", "EV-TRIP-00403"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The one route by which the driver could have added separate in-geofence intervals together is POL-NS-06(i), and it is closed on this record. That limb requires a traffic_advisory that is present and populated, of an admissible type, covering the pickup road and the waiting window. EV-ADVIS-00403-01 is MISSING - no advisory covers Gateway Dr in this window - and carries weight 0.0; the code-computed accumulation block returns 0 in-geofence intervals and no advisory candidates at all. A MISSING advisory makes limb (i) unavailable and cannot be asserted to excuse a shortfall, and POL-NS-06(ii) is express that no advisory ever reduces the required minimum. The 300 second shortfall therefore stands untouched.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00403-01", "EV-GPS-00403"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The chat log shows what actually happened. The rider's message sent at 13:27:32 named her exact position - 'taxi stand outside tower b basement 1' - which is the registered pickup point on the trip record (Westgate, 3 Gateway Dr, Jurong East, Taxi Stand Tower B B1, venue VEN-WESTGATE). The driver's reply at 13:28:07 placed him at 'the pickup bay near jem side' and told her to 'come over'; four minutes later he cancelled without moving. On those facts POL-NS-03 gives the rider the full refund, and limb (i) is directly on point: where the rider stated the correct entrance, block or tower in the chat log and the driver did not move to it before cancelling, the driver bears the loss and receives no compensation. POL-NS-03(ii)'s pin-ambiguity goodwill is not open either, because it applies only where neither party specified a sub-location and this rider named the stand, the tower and the basement level. POL-NS-04's 120 second exoneration does not apply because the driver did reply, in 35 seconds - and POL-NS-04 itself sends a replied-to mislocation to POL-NS-03.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00403", "EV-TRIP-00403"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03", "POL-NS-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Any suggestion that the rider was not there is contradicted by her own track on the same artifact as the driver's. The rider track runs from 13:26:52 to 13:32:34 with 39 fixes, all 39 of them qualifying, a mean distance of 11.3 m from the pickup pin and a maximum of only 15.2 m, at a single distinct speed of 0.0 kph. That is squarely inside the 150 m LARGE_VENUE rider presence radius, and it is stationary for the whole window down to the cancellation. The rider was at the pin and never left it; the driver was elsewhere and told her to move to him.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00403", "EV-CHAT-00403"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.max_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver cannot shortcut the geofence test with the platform's own arrival machinery. platform_policy.arrival_marker for this trip is BUTTON, not GPS_AUTO. POL-NS-12 recognises platform-confirmed arrival only from a GPS_AUTO arrival event carrying the platform's own geofence measurement with wait-timer events, and says in terms that a driver-pressed marker is not covered by it. The 13:26:52 'arrived' event is therefore nothing more than the driver's own assertion, which must be tested under POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-05 - and it does not survive the POL-NS-02 test set out above.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00403", "EV-GPS-00403"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-12"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no money for the driver on this record. POL-NS-07 compensates the driver only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it. Limb (d) fails, and POL-NS-03 and POL-NS-06 each displace it independently, so the 80 percent payout is never reached. POL-NS-03(i) separately denies compensation where the rider named the tower in chat and the driver did not move to it. Nothing in the driver's profile changes that: the anti-farming check requires no_show_terminations_30d of 4 or more and a rate above 0.08, and the driver's figure is 1, so the profile is neither a ground for nor against anyone here.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00403", "EV-CHAT-00403", "EV-DPROF-00403"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03", "POL-NS-07"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing on the rider's side of this case is impaired, so no discount applies to the facts that decide it. EV-GPS-00403 is COMPLETE at weight 1.0: 73 fixes at the 10 second expected cadence, 100 per cent coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds, so POL-NS-08(b)'s 120 second gap threshold and six-fix threshold are not engaged, and the rider track it relies on is present. EV-TRIP-00403, EV-CHAT-00403 and EV-FARE-00403 are likewise COMPLETE at weight 1.0, and the fare ledger's cancellation line of 4.00 reconciles with the net figure of 4.00 read from platform_policy through the fee schedule's resolution rule, so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged either. Under POL-GEN-02(2) the deciding facts carry weight 1.0, and nothing here drives confidence to the 0.70 floor.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00403", "EV-TRIP-00403", "EV-CHAT-00403", "EV-FARE-00403"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02", "POL-NS-08"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The sum in issue is exactly $4.00 and there is nothing else on the ledger. The fare breakdown shows a single cancellation_fee line of 4.00 against total_charged of 4.00, with payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and the waiting_time_fee line at 0.00 with no distance, time or platform components. POL-NS-06 refunds the cancellation-fee line, and under POL-GEN-03 a ruling that returns the whole contested amount to the filing party - here the rider - is FULL_REFUND, meaning the present charge is not left standing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00403", "EV-TRIP-00403"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-GEN-03"]
    },
    {
      "text": "This case should be decided, not deferred. No POL-NS-09 trigger is engaged: the driver's trace and the trip record are both COMPLETE at weight 1.0 and are not impaired under any limb of POL-NS-08, so limb (e) does not fire; the reason code in limb (d) of POL-NS-01 decides the charge whatever the arrival facts are, so there is no unresolved conflict of the kind limb (b) describes; and rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are both 0 with rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d at 0, so limbs (c) and (d) do not fire. Escalation would only hold the $4.00 the rider has already been charged; the record supports a ruling now.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00403", "EV-TRIP-00403", "EV-RPROF-00403", "EV-DPROF-00403"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09"]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the $4.00 cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-00403 is refunded in full to the rider, and no compensation is paid to the driver.\n\nThe fee cannot be charged. POL-NS-01 permits a no-show fee only if all four of its conditions hold, and its condition (d) requires the trip record to record the trip as terminated by the driver under RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT. EV-TRIP-00403 (weight 1.0, complete) records the driver cancelling at 13:32:40 under DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE. POL-NS-01 names that code as the driver's own admission that he could not find the rider and excludes it from limb (d). The charge falls on the reason code alone.\n\nThe waiting period the fee pays for was also not served. POL-NS-01(c) measures the dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix, not from the driver's 'arrived' tap, and POL-NS-12 confirms that a driver-pressed marker - arrival_marker is BUTTON on this trip - is not platform-confirmed arrival. On EV-GPS-00403 (weight 1.0, complete) the computed effective in-geofence dwell is 0.0 seconds (longest qualifying run) against the 300-second free waiting period in force for this LARGE_VENUE pickup (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec): a shortfall of 300.0 seconds. POL-NS-06 makes a shortfall of that kind a refund in full, whether or not the rider was present. The same trace records no qualifying fix inside the 120 m arrival radius at any point (qualifying_fix_count 0 of 73 driver fixes), so POL-NS-02 is not satisfied either; the driver's nearest approach of 19.8 m during the trip is a single unqualified reading, not a stationary in-radius interval.\n\nThe driver's points are answered. His claim that the trip record's 5.8-minute wait (348 seconds from the 13:26:52 arrival tap to the 13:32:40 cancellation) meets limb (c) is rejected: that interval is the marker-to-cancellation time, and POL-NS-01(c) and POL-NS-12 both measure the dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix instead. His point that the arrival counter does not publish the horizontal accuracy behind it, so it cannot be read as affirmative proof he was elsewhere, is a fair caveat and is why the ruling does not rest on POL-NS-02 alone; it does not help him, because limb (d) fails on the reason code and the dwell shortfall comes from the trace's own longest qualifying run. His escalation argument under POL-NS-09(b) is rejected: the 348 seconds and the 0.0 seconds are two different measurements and the clauses say which one is the dwell, so there is no unresolved conflict between artifacts; no other escalation trigger is engaged either - rider and driver each show 0 disputes with the other in 90 days, rider no_show_disputes_30d is 0, the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip, and the deciding artifacts are complete at weight 1.0.\n\nOn fault and the driver's money: the rider's message at 13:27:32 named her exact position, the taxi stand outside Tower B, basement 1 - the registered pickup point on the trip record (Westgate, 3 Gateway Dr, Jurong East, Taxi Stand Tower B B1). The driver answered at 13:28:07 that he was at the pickup bay 'near jem side' and asked her to come to him, and cancelled at 13:32:40 without moving to her. POL-NS-03(i) applies: the driver bears the loss and receives no compensation. The pin-ambiguity goodwill in POL-NS-03(ii) is not open to him, because it requires that neither party specified a sub-location and both did. POL-NS-07 pays a driver only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, which it is not, so no 80 percent payout arises. If the driver's stationary position was outside the arrival radius but within 400 m of the pin, POL-NS-03 gives the same result - full refund to the rider, nothing to the driver - so nothing turns on that question. His own profile supports no counter-claim: 1 no-show termination in the trailing 30 days against 120 completed trips (rate 0.008) is far below the POL-NS-07 thresholds, so no withholding or escalation arises.\n\nTwo further points. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider, because the driver replied to her message 35 seconds later and limb (b) of that clause fails; the refund does not depend on POL-NS-04, and the reply routes the mislocation question to POL-NS-03. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00403-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 and can carry no fact: it makes the POL-NS-06(i) accumulation - the driver's only route to adding separate in-geofence intervals together - unavailable, so its absence cannot help him. That claim was discarded before the hearing for not disclosing the impairment.\n\nNo referral is added. The rider asks that the mis-selected reason code be recorded as a driver-education item; POL-NS-01 directs that only where the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius, and this trace shows no in-geofence stationary interval at all (0 runs, 0.0 seconds), so that limb is not reached. POL-NS-05 is not engaged either: the package does not publish the driver's position or speed at the 13:26:52 marker, so no false-arrival finding can be made and the POL-NS-05(ii) referral does not fire. No other clause produces a referral on these facts. Nothing in this ruling rests on a profile field that POL-GEN-01 makes context only; rating, cancellation rate and account age are not used.\n\nThe figures are read from EV-FARE-00403: the single cancellation_fee line is 4.00, total_charged 4.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and the waiting-time line 0.00; the 4.00 matches the net figure from platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd through the fee schedule, so the ledger reconciles and POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged. The refund is therefore 4.00 and the ruling is FULL_REFUND. Confidence is 0.95: the deciding facts rest on artifacts at weight 1.0 (EV-TRIP-00403, EV-GPS-00403, EV-FARE-00403), so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0, and the bundle mean is not the cap. The monetary effect, 4.00, is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of 8.00, so it is executed automatically on issue; either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The one route by which the driver could have added separate in-geofence intervals together is POL-NS-06(i), and it is closed on this record. That limb requires a traffic_advisory that is present and populated, of an admissible type, covering the pickup road and the waiting window. EV-ADVIS-00403-01 is MISSING - no advisory covers Gateway Dr in this window - and carries weight 0.0; the code-computed accumulation block returns 0 in-geofence intervals and no advisory candidates at all. A MISSING advisory makes limb (i) unavailable and cannot be asserted to excuse a shortfall, and POL-NS-06(ii) is express that no advisory ever reduces the required minimum. The 300 second shortfall therefore stands untouched.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00403-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
